201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This strategy works best on the 4-hour timeframe. The 4-hour chart helps catch clean swing moves and filters out extra noise found on lower timeframes. A top-down look at bigger timeframes, like the daily or weekly, helps confirm the main trend direction. The 4-hour chart is then used to draw trend lines, find touchpoints, and plan entries and exits. This keeps the setups clear and consistent.)
/E (This strategy works best on the 4-hour timeframe. The 4-hour chart helps catch clean swing moves and filters out extra noise found on lower timeframes. A top-down look at bigger timeframes, like the daily or weekly, helps confirm the main trend direction. The 4-hour chart is then used to draw trend lines, find touchpoints, and plan entries and exits. This keeps the setups clear and consistent.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
